# Bubble Sort Array Example

This project demonstrates how to sort an array using the bubble sort algorithm in C++.

## Files
- `main.cpp` - contains the program logic and the bubble sort function

## How to run
1. Open `37.BroCodHowToSortArayBubleMyNts.sln` in Visual Studio
2. Build the solution
3. Press F5 to run

//For purposes of lesson use four values to demonstrate and write comments to update the ones already present.
//Bubble sorts can contain as many values as needed.
## Example
The program starts with an unsorted array:
`10, 1, 9, 4`

After sorting, it prints:
`1, 4, 9, 10`

Extra:

If you would like another example of a bubble sort but in the C language (very similar):

